{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5478-1","published":"2026-11-26T15:23:00Z","modified":"2026-11-27T11:01:29.289318691Z","related":["CVE-2026-53615","CVE-2026-76642","CVE-2026-78408","CVE-2026-78409","CVE-2026-78410"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-53615","CVE-2026-76642","CVE-2026-78408","CVE-2026-78409","CVE-2026-78410"],"summary":"Security update for util-linux","details":"This update for util-linux fixes the following issues:\n\nSecurity issues fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-53615: integer overflow in `parse_dos_extended()` due to missing bounds check allows a crafted disk image\n  or removable media to cause `libblkid` to register a partition at sector 0 (bsc#1285600).\n- CVE-2026-76642: failed external mount helper triggers privileged `X-mount` post-hooks, which enables local privilege\n  escalation (bsc#1278349).\n- CVE-2026-78408: `nsenter --join-cgroup` leaks root `cgroup` migration authority, which allows for migration or\n  termination of root processes (bsc#1278348).\n- CVE-2026-78409: `X-mount.subdir` uses unsafe detached-tree resolution, which allows for filesystem escape via\n  intermediate symlinks and `procfs` paths (bsc#1278346).\n- CVE-2026-78410: restricted `bind` mounts do not pin the source, which allows for `X-mount.owner`/`group`/`mode`\n  redirection (bsc#1278347).\n\nOther updates and bugfixes:\n\n- Fixed user mounts refused under user-writable parent, reports misleading 'special device tmpfs does not exist'\n  (bsc#1282799).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"util-linux","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 15 SP6-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/util-linux&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2015%20SP6-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.39.3-150600.4.29.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libblkid-devel":"2.39.3-150600.4.29.1","libblkid-devel-static":"2.39.3-150600.4.29.1","libblkid1":"2.39.3-150600.4.29.1","libblkid1-32bit":"2.39.3-150600.4.29.1","libfdisk-devel":"2.39.3-150600.4.29.1","libf